---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { config } from '../config';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  type="profile"
  description={config.bio}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
  schema={[{ '@type': 'ProfilePage', '@id': `${config.url}/about/#profile`, url: `${config.url}/about/`, name: `About ${config.name}`, mainEntity: { '@id': `${config.url}/#person` }, isPartOf: { '@id': `${config.url}/#website` } }]}
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="tagline" style="font:italic 1.4rem var(--display);color:var(--accent)">{config.tagline}</p>
  <p>I'm {config.name}, based in {config.location}. {config.bio}</p>
  <p>I spent a decade-plus in data: pipelines, warehouses, the unglamorous plumbing that decides whether anything downstream works. Agents turned out to have the same failure modes with more personality. <em>(Placeholder: replace with your own story.)</em></p>
  <h2>What I write about</h2>
  <ul>{config.topics.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}</ul>
  <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={config.links.github} rel="me">GitHub</a></li>
    <li><a href={config.links.linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn</a></li>
    <li><a href={config.links.hashnode} rel="me">Hashnode</a> (cross-posts; this site is the canonical home)</li>
    <li><a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Need help getting agents into production? See <a href="/work-with-me/">working with me</a>.</p>
</Base>
